-- When a compound breach happened, and who decided it (SEESAW, 2026-10-09).
--
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC section 6.1.2. Each failure a breach names
-- carries two instants: when it took EFFECT (a missed deadline, never earlier
-- than the obligation's own arming; a violating act's stamp; a declared
-- BREACH's hand-off clock) and when it was OBSERVED (the stamp of the event
-- that revealed it). A RAND is breached at the earliest effective instant of
-- its operands, an ROR at the latest, worked out along the operand tree; the
-- entries that fix that instant are the DECISIVE ones. Every pair below is
-- written both ways round and must report the same instant and the same
-- decisive entries; only the order of the list (the drafter's) differs.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF P, Q, R
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF x, y, z, w

-- §1 Nesting. (P by 1 ROR Q by 10) RAND R by 5: the ROR holds until 10, so
-- the RAND is lost at 5, by R. Not at 1: P's miss broke nothing while Q was
-- still open. One event at 11 reveals all three misses at once.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`p or q` MEANS (PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 1) ROR (PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`q or p` MEANS (PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 10) ROR (PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 1)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`r by 5` MEANS PARTY R MUST z WITHIN 5

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`or, then and` MEANS `p or q` RAND `r by 5`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`and, then or` MEANS `r by 5` RAND `q or p`

#TRACE `or, then and` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 11)

#TRACE `and, then or` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 11)

-- Three events instead of one: the same answer.
#TRACE `or, then and` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 2)
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 6)
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 11)

#TRACE `and, then or` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 2)
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 6)
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 11)

-- §2 Two misses at one instant. Both due at 5, one event at 10: both entries
-- are decisive.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`both due at 5` MEANS (PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 5) RAND (PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 5)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`both due at 5, swapped` MEANS (PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 5) RAND (PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `both due at 5` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `both due at 5, swapped` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- §3 A missed deadline beside a declared BREACH at the same instant. Q's
-- LEST BREACH takes effect at Q's deadline, 5, the instant P misses too.
-- Neither kind wins by position: the report is a missed deadline (not every
-- decisive entry is declared), and both entries are decisive.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`miss` MEANS PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 5

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`declared` MEANS PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 5 LEST BREACH BY Q BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`miss and declared` MEANS `miss` RAND `declared`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`declared and miss` MEANS `declared` RAND `miss`

#TRACE `miss and declared` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `declared and miss` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- §4 An obligation armed after its own deadline. P acts at 4, which arms R's
-- obligation; its WITHIN 3 OF THE ARMING counts from the arming of the
-- obligation it continues (P's, at 0), so R is due at 3 and armed at 4. It
-- could never be met: the run says so in a note, and the failure takes
-- effect at 4, not 3. Q's miss at 3.5 therefore comes first.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`late arming` MEANS
    PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY R MUST z WITHIN 3 OF THE ARMING)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`q by 3.5` MEANS PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 3.5

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`late arming and q` MEANS `late arming` RAND `q by 3.5`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`q and late arming` MEANS `q by 3.5` RAND `late arming`

#TRACE `late arming and q` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 3.8)
  PARTY P DOES x AT 4
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

#TRACE `q and late arming` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 3.8)
  PARTY P DOES x AT 4
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

-- §5 A kept prohibition hands its HENCE the end of its window (5), however
-- many idle events the trace carries before the next one. R is due at 6 in
-- both traces.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`kept, then R` MEANS PARTY P SHANT x WITHIN 5 HENCE (PARTY R MUST z WITHIN 1)

#TRACE `kept, then R` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `kept, then R` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 6)
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A declared BREACH in that HENCE takes effect at 5 too, so beside Q's miss
-- at 7 it decides the RAND, whichever side it is on and however many events
-- came between.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`kept, then breach` MEANS PARTY P SHANT x WITHIN 5 HENCE BREACH BY P BECAUSE "kept"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`q by 7` MEANS PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 7

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`kept breach and q` MEANS `kept, then breach` RAND `q by 7`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`q and kept breach` MEANS `q by 7` RAND `kept, then breach`

#TRACE `kept breach and q` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `q and kept breach` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `kept breach and q` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 6)
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- §6 ROR: breached only when the last alternative fails. A lapsed MAY's bare
-- LEST BREACH takes effect at the MAY's deadline (5), Q's miss at 7: the ROR
-- is lost at 7, by Q; the RAND at 5, by the BREACH.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`may lapses` MEANS PARTY P MAY x WITHIN 5 LEST BREACH

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`may or q` MEANS `may lapses` ROR `q by 7`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`q or may` MEANS `q by 7` ROR `may lapses`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`may and q` MEANS `may lapses` RAND `q by 7`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`q and may` MEANS `q by 7` RAND `may lapses`

#TRACE `may or q` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `q or may` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `may and q` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `q and may` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- §7 One BREACH reached twice. `oops` is shared; reached at 5 on the left and
-- at 9 on the right, each reach takes its own instant: the left RAND is lost
-- at 5, the right at 7 (Q's miss beats the reach at 9), so the ROR is lost
-- at 7, by Q.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`oops` MEANS BREACH BY P BECAUSE "shared"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`left half` MEANS (PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 5 LEST `oops`) RAND (PARTY Q MUST w WITHIN 100)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`right half` MEANS (PARTY R MUST z WITHIN 9 LEST `oops`) RAND (PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 7)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`whole` MEANS `left half` ROR `right half`

#TRACE `whole` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 200)

-- §8 A barrier is a RAND over the members that failed. P is due at 5 and Q
-- at 3, and one event at 10 reveals both: the group is lost at 3, by Q, the
-- same answer the RAND of the two obligations gives.

ps MEANS LIST P, Q

GIVEN t IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days for` t MEANS IF t EQUALS P THEN 5 ELSE 3

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`everyone` MEANS
    EVERY t IN ps
        MUST   x
        WITHIN `days for` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the pair` MEANS (PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 5) RAND (PARTY Q MUST x WITHIN 3)

#TRACE `everyone` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

#TRACE `the pair` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- §9 A broken prohibition has a join: under its LEST, THE JOIN is the act
-- that broke it. P does x at 3, so the fine is due 3 + 2 = 5, and the tick
-- at 6 shows it missed.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`broken, then fined` MEANS
    PARTY P SHANT x WITHIN 10
    LEST  (PARTY P MUST w WITHIN 2 OF THE JOIN)

#TRACE `broken, then fined` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY P DOES x AT 3
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 6)
